.TH OMX-RTA-READ 1 2026-11-15 omx-dsp "OpenMixer"
.SH NAME
omx-rta-read \- the spectrum of a JACK signal, read and never fed
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B omx-rta-read
[\fB\-\-post\fR \fIport\fR]... [\fB\-\-pre\fR \fIport\fR]... \fB\-\-bands\fR \fIn\fR
[\fB\-\-low\fR] [\fB\-\-name\fR \fIclient\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
omx-rta-read reads the spectrum of a processor's signal in a JACK graph and
writes it as log-spaced bands, one JSON line at a time, for a panel to draw.
It is a JACK client with input ports only, connected only FROM the ports it
watches: it never feeds anything.
.PP
Two taps, each of one or two legs (a pair is read as its mono sum).
\fB\-\-post\fR names an output port of the processor: what it gives.
\fB\-\-pre\fR names an INPUT port of the processor: the reader connects from
every port connected to it, which is what the processor is given, and follows
the graph when that set changes. A tap is read only when it is named.
.PP
Its process callback writes each leg's period into omx-dsp's capture ring and
nothing else; omx-rt-gate(1) judges it whole (\fB\-\-abi jack\fR). Ten times a
second, once every leg holds a whole window of audio since the connect, both
taps are read at one frame position, reduced to \fIn\fR bands by omx-dsp's
omx_rta_bands (the window, the bands, the tier crossover and the quiet gate
are omx-dsp's declared numbers) and written:
.PP
.RS
{"at":\fIframes\fR,"rate":\fIHz\fR,"hz":[...],"post":{"db":[...],"peak":[...]},"pre":{...}}
.RE
.PP
each band's centre in Hz, its level (the RMS across its bins) and its peak (its
loudest bin) in dBFS to 0.01, silence as null; a tap's object only when it is
read. Before the first whole window nothing is written.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-post " port"
An output port to read. Twice for a stereo pair.
.TP
.BI \-\-pre " port"
An input port whose feeders to read. Twice for a stereo pair.
.TP
.BI \-\-bands " n"
The number of bands, 1 to 1024.
.TP
.B \-\-low
Also read the low zoom (an eighth of the rate, eight times the resolution) and
use it for the bands under the crossover.
.TP
.BI \-\-name " client"
The JACK client name (default omx-rta-read).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on SIGTERM or SIGINT; 2 a usage error; 3 its standard output closed (the
reader of the pipe is gone); 4 a watched port is gone; 5 the JACK server is
gone; 6 the server refused the client or a connection. The reason is written
on standard error.
.SH SEE ALSO
omx-rt-gate(1)
